# VOLUMES (rmbp-ledger B366) M3 — `system/test-f/`: one FREE sample of every format the kernel claims, staged by the
# builder onto the DATA volume (and by `arroyo esp-x86` onto the card's UnaFS root at /system/test-f). Peter, flight 22:
# "maybe you can find free samples for all the various file format we need tested?" / "we need test-f under system".
#
# <staged name> <sha256 | -> <licence> <source>
#   fetched rows: fetched at image time into target/testf-cache/ (curl), refused unless the sha256 is the pin.
#     BSD-3-Clause (Chromium) = the Chromium project's test data (github.com/chromium/chromium LICENSE); the audio
#     and AV1 rows are the very files libs/media/*/tests/vectors.txt already fetch for the oracles.
#     bmpsuite (public domain) = Jason Summers' BMP Suite, as carried by image-rs/image's tests.
#   generated rows (sha `-`): written by the builder itself (builder/src/main.rs `testf_generated`), CC0-1.0.
# The set is < 1 MB (20 MB is the ceiling). `tests testf` on the running kernel lists staged vs claimed.
